/-!
# §6.2 Lemma 16: the positional layout permutation `L`

Record addresses are lists of address bits (shape `replicate n 2`); every bit position holds a
*named slot* (a natural-number name, `nm i h` for slot `h` of axis `i`). Two kinds of primitive
moves act on positions:

* `LOp.mv c p` — move the bit at position `p ≥ c` to position `c` (the single-field move of
  Lemma 3, `rotIdx` of `AModelL12Basic`);
* `LOp.xch i j K` — exchange two width-`K` address chunks (`blockSwap`; by `pull_blockSwap` this is
  the chunk interchange of Lemma 12, `lemma12_bit`, on the merged shape).

`applyN ops arr` is the resulting arrangement of slot names, `runArr ops xs` the array
denotation (each primitive is the `pull` by the inverse position map).

* `runArr_eq_pull` (**denotation**): `runArr ops xs = pull (relabel init (applyN ops init))`:
  the composite moves the record whose slot values are `v` from the address with slots in the
  initial order to the address with slots in the final order (`relabel`).
* `prefix_moves`: listed slots can be moved one by one to a prefix with `|Lst|` single moves,
  leaving the others in order.
* `chunk_sort`: any rearrangement of `n` distinct `K`-chunks by at most `n - 1` exchanges.
-/

